+# WGAN-GP — reproduction record
+
+A clean-room reproduction of `implementations/wgan_gp` from
+[eriklindernoren/PyTorch-GAN](https://github.com/eriklindernoren/PyTorch-GAN)
+(MIT), run for the **Reproducible AI** campaign.
+
+We claim **reproduce, not replicate**: the goal is that the published pipeline
+runs end to end from a clean checkout, that every input and output is recorded
+in lineage, and that a metric is actually computed. It is **not** a claim about
+sample quality or about matching any published number.
+
+* Upstream: <https://github.com/eriklindernoren/PyTorch-GAN> — MIT, © 2018 Erik Linder-Norén
+* Fork used for this run: <https://github.com/reproducible-ai/PyTorch-GAN>
+* Model: `hf://reproducible-ai/pytorch-gan-wgangp`
+* Dataset: MNIST (train split for training, **test** split for evaluation)
+
+## The run
+
+**TRUNCATED — 3 epochs, upstream's default is 200. The checkpoint is not
+converged** and is published as a provenance artifact, not a quality result.
+
+Workflow: [`.treqs/workflows/pytorch-gan-wgangp.yaml`](../../.treqs/workflows/pytorch-gan-wgangp.yaml)
+
+| Step | Command | Writes |
+|---|---|---|
+| `prepare` | `python implementations/wgan_gp/prepare_data.py --data_root data/mnist` | `data/mnist/` |
+| `train` | `python implementations/wgan_gp/wgan_gp.py --n_epochs 3 --seed 42 --data_root data/mnist --sample_dir samples --checkpoint out/wgangp.pt` | `out/wgangp.pt`, `samples/` |
+| `evaluate` | `python implementations/wgan_gp/eval_wgan_gp.py --checkpoint out/wgangp.pt --data_root data/mnist --metrics metrics/metrics.json` | `metrics/metrics.json` |
+
+All four output directories — `data/`, `samples/`, `out/`, `metrics/` — are
+tracked directories (each holds a committed `.gitkeep`) whose contents are
+gitignored, so a clean checkout has somewhere to put them and the working tree
+stays clean between steps.
+
+### Metrics computed
+
+`evaluate` loads the published checkpoint and computes, on MNIST's **test**
+split (unseen during training):
+
+* mean critic score on real images,
+* mean critic score on generated images,
+* the Wasserstein-distance estimate `E[D(real)] − E[D(fake)]`,
+* the WGAN-GP gradient penalty.
+
+## Modifications to upstream
+
+Every change is listed here. Upstream behaviour is preserved when the new flags
+are omitted — running `python wgan_gp.py` with no arguments does exactly what it
+did before.
+
+### `wgan_gp.py` (modified)
+
+1. **A checkpoint is now saved.** *Upstream saves none* — the trained generator
+   and critic are discarded when the process exits, so nothing can be published,
+   evaluated or re-used. Added `--checkpoint PATH`; when set, the final
+   generator and discriminator `state_dict`s, the parsed argparse config,
+   `img_shape`, `lambda_gp` and the batch count are written with `torch.save`.
+   Default `""` = save nothing = upstream behaviour.
+2. **Output paths are configurable.** Added `--data_root` (default
+   `../../data/mnist`, upstream's literal) and `--sample_dir` (default `images`,
+   upstream's literal). Upstream hard-coded both, and both were relative to the
+   *process* working directory, so the script could only be launched from
+   `implementations/wgan_gp/`. Configurable paths let the pipeline run from the
+   repository root and keep every artifact inside the repo.
+3. **`os.makedirs("images")` moved below `parse_args()`.** Upstream ran it at
+   import time — before the options existed — which is why the sample directory
+   could not be configured.
+4. **Added `--seed`** (default `-1` = unseeded = upstream behaviour). Upstream
+   seeds nothing, so two runs of the same commit differ. The campaign run passes
+   `--seed 42`.
+
+### `prepare_data.py` (added)
+
+Downloads MNIST as its own step. Upstream fetches the dataset as a side effect
+of building the `DataLoader` inside the training script, which makes the dataset
+look like something *training* produced rather than something it consumed.
+
+### `eval_wgan_gp.py` (added)
+
+Loads the checkpoint and computes the metrics above. The `Generator` and
+`Discriminator` classes are copied from `wgan_gp.py` because upstream defines
+them at module scope next to the training loop, so they cannot be imported
+without also running training. `load_state_dict(..., strict=True)` makes any
+future drift between the two copies fail loudly instead of silently evaluating a
+different network.
+
+## Upstream observations
+
+Findings about the upstream implementation, recorded as-is. None of them were
+"fixed" here — this is a reproduction, not an improvement.
+
+1. **No checkpoint is ever written.** After up to 200 epochs the model is thrown
+   away. `implementations/wgan_gp/` produces only PNG grids.
+2. **`nn.BatchNorm1d(out_feat, 0.8)` passes `0.8` as `eps`, not `momentum`.**
+   `BatchNorm1d`'s signature is `(num_features, eps=1e-5, momentum=0.1, ...)`,
+   so the second positional argument is the epsilon. `0.8` is ~5 orders of
+   magnitude above the default epsilon and heavily damps the normalisation;
+   `momentum=0.8` is the far more plausible intent. The same call appears across
+   many implementations in the repository.
+3. **`--n_cpu` is dead.** It is parsed and documented as "number of cpu threads
+   to use during batch generation", but the `DataLoader` is constructed without
+   `num_workers`, so the value is never used.
+4. **`--clip_value` is dead in this implementation.** Weight clipping is the
+   *WGAN* mechanism that WGAN-GP's gradient penalty replaces; the flag is
+   inherited from `implementations/wgan/` and has no effect here.
+5. **`requirements.txt` is unpinned and effectively stale** (`torch>=0.4.0`,
+   plus bare `torchvision`, `numpy`, `scipy`, `pillow`, `urllib3`,
+   `scikit-image`). It admits every PyTorch release from 2018 to today, so it
+   does not describe an environment that can be rebuilt. It also lists
+   dependencies this implementation does not use.
+6. **`torch.autograd.Variable` is used throughout.** Deprecated since PyTorch
+   0.4; it still works as an alias for `Tensor` but is dead weight.
+7. **The repository-level `.gitignore` contains `*.json`,** which silently
+   ignores any metrics or config file written at the default paths.
+8. **The generator is updated using the critic's noise batch.** In the
+   `i % n_critic == 0` branch, `z` is reused from the discriminator step rather
+   than resampled. This is a defensible choice, not a bug, but it is undocumented
+   and differs from the reference WGAN-GP algorithm.
+
+## Rebuilding
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/reproducible-ai/PyTorch-GAN
+cd PyTorch-GAN
+python implementations/wgan_gp/prepare_data.py --data_root data/mnist
+python implementations/wgan_gp/wgan_gp.py --n_epochs 3 --seed 42 \
+    --data_root data/mnist --sample_dir samples --checkpoint out/wgangp.pt
+python implementations/wgan_gp/eval_wgan_gp.py --checkpoint out/wgangp.pt \
+    --data_root data/mnist --metrics metrics/metrics.json
+```
+
+## License
+
+Upstream is MIT (`LICENSE`, © 2018 Erik Linder-Norén); this fork and the
+modifications above are MIT as well.
